    "gate-open": {
      "id": "gate-open",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The quality gate decides whether a worker submission can become a selectable checkpoint. The runner checks the actual diff, compilation, match measurements, scope, and lint rules. The worker's claimed score cannot approve its own result."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "gate-hard": {
      "id": "gate-hard",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Every submission is checked again. A 100% match that fails a hard gate is rejected and returned with repair feedback. A gate-clean improvement can be banked while the same worker continues. Selection and integration occur separately."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "ec5547d8-3805-40ca-9772-e375bb59f0e7": {
      "id": "ec5547d8-3805-40ca-9772-e375bb59f0e7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Before the first attempt the runner builds the target object at baseline and records the pre-worker measurement. Object, symbol, and split paths come from the game's build layout, derived from the configured report path ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "build/<version>/...",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "config/<version>/...",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), so a second game never inherits another game's target names. If that baseline build fails, nothing the worker could do would validate: the runner closes the worker as an infrastructure error ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "baseline_build_failed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") without launching an agent, re-admits the target for another worker under the consecutive infrastructure-failure cap, and records the build output for diagnosis."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "gate-checks": {
      "id": "gate-checks",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "What the Runner Checks"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "gate-process": {
      "id": "gate-process",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Validate one submission",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Capture the diff and check claim-authorized paths"
              },
              {
                "text": "Compile and measure the target and required affected scope"
              },
              {
                "text": "Run QA lint, review-diff lint, and configured post-return checks"
              },
              {
                "text": "Record scores, hard-gate results, artifacts, and failure reasons"
              },
              {
                "text": "Return repair feedback or preserve an eligible checkpoint"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "gate-review": {
      "id": "gate-review",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Review here is the runner's validation path, including deterministic review-diff lint. A submission must pass runner validation and avoid failed review lint before "
        },
        {
          "insert": "hardGatesPassed",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " can be true. Rejection identifies the failing checks so the same worker can repair its next submission."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "gate-lint": {
      "id": "gate-lint",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Deterministic Lint"
        }
