    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-attempt-budget-intro-70": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-attempt-budget-intro-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Continuation runs one unified attempt budget ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "attempt_budget_v3",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "WORKER_ATTEMPT_BUDGET_POLICY",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker-cycle.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). A worker gets 5 base submissions, and a submission that sets a strictly new best qualifying score grants +2 budget. A qualifying score is a finite score from a selectable checkpoint that passed hard gates and improved over baseline. Any exact match also qualifies, including one that failed hard gates. Repeated gate-failed exacts grant only once, and a score below the running best grants nothing. After each attempt "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workerContinuationDecision",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " replays the checkpoint history and applies the checks below in order."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-attempt-budget-grants-71": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-attempt-budget-grants-71",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A banked improvement keeps the worker open. The checkpoint is durable in SQLite the moment it is recorded, so the worker keeps pushing toward exact, and each new best extends the budget by two attempts. A gate-failed 100% spends its remaining budget trying to become gate-clean; if it never does, the worker closes normally and the best selectable checkpoint is selected, or the baseline if no checkpoint is selectable. Budget extends attempts only, never time: the claim TTL is stamped at claim time as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent_timeout_seconds",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " plus a 600-second grace, each attempt's Pi session gets "
        },
        {
          "insert": "agent_timeout_seconds",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and the job process is killed at the TTL."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
